                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V/G \to \mathbf{B}G
              and when
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              is (necessarily)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
              basepoint of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
              gives the desired action on the desired type.
            %p
              First of all, we have the composite
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi A
                      %mi Type
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ♯
                      %msub
                        %mi Type
                        %mo ♯
