          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            Actions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} A-∞ algebras
            in some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-category
            are discussed in section 4.2 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebra"} Higher Algebra
          %p
            The discussion of
            = succeed "-actions" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul
            %li#NSS
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"}> Thomas Nikolaus
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Danny+Stevenson"} Danny Stevenson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles+--+theory%2C+presentations+and+applications"} Principal ∞-bundles – theory, presentations and applications
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1207.0248"} arXiv:1207.0248
            %li#SatiSchreiber20
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Proper+Orbifold+Cohomology"} Proper Orbifold Cohomology
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.01101"}> arXiv:2008.01101
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#SatiSchreiber21
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Equivariant+principal+infinity-bundles"}
                    Equivariant principal
                    = succeed "-bundles" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.13654"}> arXiv:2112.13654
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Discussion in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li#BuchholtzDoornRijke18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrik+Buchholtz"}> Ulrik Buchholtz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Floris+van+Doorn"} Floris van Doorn
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"} Egbert Rijke
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher Groups in Homotopy Type Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.04315"} arXiv:1802.04315
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1145/3209108.3209150"} doi:10.1145/3209108.3209150
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrik+Buchholtz"}> Ulrik Buchholtz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Notes on higher groups and projective spaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www2.mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de/~buchholtz/higher-groups.pdf"} pdf
          %p On extensions of actions on a space to actions on geometric structures defined over it:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Severin+Bunk"}> Severin Bunk
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+S.+Shahbazi"} Carlos S. Shahbazi
              %em Higher Geometric Structures on Manifolds and the Gauge Theory of Deligne Cohomology
              (2023). (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.06633"}> arXiv:2304.06633
              ).
          %h3#ReferencesForDiscreteGeometry For discrete geometry
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}= \infty Grpd
            the statement that homotopy types over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
            are equivalently
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-actions"} infinity-actions
            is (via the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+model+structure"} Borel model structure
          %ul
            %li#DDK80
              E. Dror,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"} William Dwyer
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant maps which are self homotopy equivalences
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/2043448"} jstor:2043448
          %p This is mentioned for instance as exercise 4.2 in
          %ul
            %li#Dwyer2008
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy theory of classifying spaces
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.ku.dk/~jg/homotopical2008/Dwyer.CopenhagenNotes.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            An alternative proof in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+categories"} relative categories
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Sharma15
              Amit Sharma,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  On the homotopy theory of
                  = succeed "-spaces" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1512.03698"} arXiv:1512.03698
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.ijmsi.org/Papers/Volume.7.Issue.2/H07025255.pdf"} published pdf
          %p
            Closely related discussion of homotopy fiber sequences and homotopy action but in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+spaces"} Segal spaces
            is in section 5 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matan+Prezma"}> Matan Prezma
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy normal maps
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1011.4708v9"} arXiv:1011.4708
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.agt/1513715387"} euclid:agt/1513715387
          %p
            There, conditions are given for a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo •
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet \to B_\bullet
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+Segal+space"} reduced Segal space
            to have a fixed homotopy fiber, and hence encode an action of the loop group of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            on that fiber.
          %h3#ForActionsOfTopologicalGroups For actions of topological groups
          %p
            That
            = succeed "-actions" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            in the sense of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-spaces"} G-spaces
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            (and hence with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %em not
            regarded as the geometrically discrete
